within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01M_QuinoloneAntibacterials.J01MA14_Moxifloxacin;
model Moxifloxacin "Moxifloxacin — default model: Moxifloxacin_Greenberg2022_reference"
  extends Moxifloxacin_Greenberg2022_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of moxifloxacin: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01M_QuinoloneAntibacterials.J01MA14_Moxifloxacin.Moxifloxacin_Greenberg2022_reference\">Moxifloxacin_Greenberg2022_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of moxifloxacin in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Moxifloxacin_Greenberg2022_reference</code></li></ul><h4>About moxifloxacin</h4><p>Moxifloxacin is a fluoroquinolone antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections such as pneumonia, sinusitis, bronchitis, conjunctivitis, and urinary tract infections. It is an approved medicine, included on the WHO essential medicines list, and is used both systemically and as eye drops, though it carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q424940\">Wikidata Q424940</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Moxifloxacin\">Moxifloxacin</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 122400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Moxifloxacin;
